"id":2650802944,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eAAsA","user":{"login":"HydrogenC","id":33123710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTIzNzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33123710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC","html_url":"https://github.com/HydrogenC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T13:16:06Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T13:18:32Z","body":"> Does this close:\r\n> \r\n> * [Add a post-light function in the spatial shader, so that proper cel shading can be done godot-proposals#484](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/484)\r\n\r\nYes, I edited the description of the P.R. just now, adding two associated issues.  \r\nBesides, the current implementation is quite casual, maybe a better design could be came up with as for where in the shader to put the post light at and which built-ins to expose to the post light function. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2650802944/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651095098","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2651095098","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2651095098,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eBIA6","user":{"login":"mk56-spn","id":74463310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDYzMzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74463310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn","html_url":"https://github.com/mk56-spn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mk56-spn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T15:05:56Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T15:06:05Z","body":"Out of curiosity , does this come with a notable performance cost when not being used?\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651095098/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651965995","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2651965995","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2651965995,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eEcor","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T20:12:32Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T20:12:32Z","body":"Great work! The trick with this has always been what to do for the compatibility renderer. We have discussed it a few times and never agreed on something that we are happy with. When using additive lighting, a \"post light\" function would stop working correctly. But we can't add a built-in shader function that only works on 2 of the 3 backends.  \r\n\r\nDo you have any thoughts on how the compatibility renderer could be supported?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651965995/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652308244","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2652308244","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2652308244,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eFwMU","user":{"login":"HydrogenC","id":33123710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTIzNzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33123710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC","html_url":"https://github.com/HydrogenC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T23:44:01Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T23:45:02Z","body":"> Out of curiosity , does this come with a notable performance cost when not being used?\r\n\r\nNope, it has no effect on the generated shader source if `post_light` isn't defined thanks to conditional compilation. \r\n\r\n\r\n> Do you have any thoughts on how the compatibility renderer could be supported?\r\n\r\nI did made it work on my local machine when I was testing. The only problem is that the compatibility shader uses two-stage tonemapping/gamma-correction. It tonemaps the base `frag_color` and the `additive_light` separately and add them together. If the tonemapping process could be merged into one then there's no problem with compatibility. I'll try if merging the tonemapping process into one would break existing visual effects. \r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652308244/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652732881","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2652732881","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2652732881,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eHX3R","user":{"login":"HydrogenC","id":33123710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTIzNzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33123710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC","html_url":"https://github.com/HydrogenC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-12T05:53:52Z","updated_at":"2025-02-12T05:53:52Z","body":"> Do you have any thoughts on how the compatibility renderer could be supported?\r\n\r\nI added the support for compatibility at of cost of potential tiny visual changes of existing shader code. \r\n\r\nOriginal logic: \r\n```\r\nfrag_color -----exposure------tonemap-----→(+)---------→final result\r\n                                            ↑\r\nadditive_light-----exposure---tonemap-------|\r\n```\r\nNew logic: \r\n```\r\n(frag_color + additive_light)----exposure----tonemap----→final result\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe exposure step is a linear transform so no difference will be introduced, but since tonemapping is non-linear, this change might have introduced tiny visual changes on color. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652732881/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652745151","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2652745151","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2652745151,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eHa2_","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-12T06:04:15Z","updated_at":"2025-02-12T06:04:15Z","body":"@HydrogenC I think you have mistaken how additive lighting works. Only the first shadowed light is included in the base pass. After that the mesh is redrawn with the blend mode set to additive and only the lighting is output to screen. This blends multiple lights in several passes. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652745151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652756463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2652756463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2652756463,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eHdnv","user":{"login":"HydrogenC","id":33123710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTIzNzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33123710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC","html_url":"https://github.com/HydrogenC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-12T06:12:36Z","updated_at":"2025-02-12T06:12:36Z","body":"> @HydrogenC I think you have mistaken how additive lighting works. Only the first shadowed light is included in the base pass. After that the mesh is redrawn with the blend mode set to additive and only the lighting is output to screen. This blends multiple lights in several passes.\r\n\r\nOh, I've mistaken it, thanks for your explanation. This makes the problem difficult, that we would need another additional pass after all lights are calculated to implement `post_light`. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652756463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652886142","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2652886142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2652886142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eH9R-","user":{"login":"HydrogenC","id":33123710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTIzNzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33123710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC","html_url":"https://github.com/HydrogenC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-12T07:40:15Z","updated_at":"2025-02-12T07:44:49Z","body":"I made a primitive implementation for compatibility which look quite consistent with other pipelines in my test case (and doesn't break support for fog and tonemapping). \r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ec92a46-ee63-4a43-8697-4cffc33c5d08)\r\n\r\nHowever there's technical limitations in multi-pass light, that users will not be able to access the accumulated `DIFFUSE_LIGHT` or `SPECULAR_LIGHT` in the implementation for compatibility, because that they are not separately stored but instead added to the final image. But it's capable of post-mapping the final color. Moreover users could use self-defined varyings to accumulate lighting data and achieve the same lighting effect as in forward implementations, as a workaround. A better and more feature-complete implementation would require <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/8050>. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652886142/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2786605293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2786605293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2786605293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mGDjt","user":{"login":"michaelharmonart","id":15620900,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjIwOTAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15620900?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelharmonart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T14:16:04Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T14:16:04Z","body":"> But we can't add a built-in shader function that only works on 2 of the 3 backends.\r\n\r\nYeah adding another descepency between the backends is toughz I already know a few that have bit me before, for instance the depth range being 0 to 1 in the RD backends and -1 to 1 in compatibility. There are also certain derivative functions or modes settings for the derivative node in the visual shader) that only work for RD backends\r\n\r\nas users do we have a way to write shaders that behave different/use different blocks of code depending on the backend?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2786605293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2786612351","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2786612351","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2786612351,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mGFR_","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T14:18:09Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T14:18:09Z","body":"> as users do we have a way to write shaders that behave different/use different blocks of code depending on the backend?\r\n\r\nYep! https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shader_preprocessor.html#current-renderer","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2786612351/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2803751002","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102708#issuecomment-2803751002","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102708","id":2803751002,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nHdha","user":{"login":"HydrogenC","id":33123710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTIzNzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33123710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC","html_url":"https://github.com/HydrogenC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T04:24:12Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T04:25:13Z","body":"After browsing godot proposals I discovered this thread (<https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/8366>) which could supersede the feature being proposed in this PR. It says \"Modifying colors after lighting happens\" which is exactly a superset of the problem this PR is intended to solve. The PR associated with that proposal (<https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94427>) is a good start but it doesn't allow sampling a custom uniform texture after lighting is calculated (since I cannot define new uniforms in the shader template yet), which is required for toon shading (\"ramp\" texture). But that's OK, now we just have to wait for that feature to be improved over time and eventually become flexible and customizable enough of solving the problem proposed by this feature request. So I close this PR for now. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2803751002/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]